(7593502, 1223676, 181335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i> This was so nearly correct, but it did not come together correctly. I think for this shot, with the soft buildings (as <img alt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=114285" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Neat</a> pointed out) it would have worked with the other overlay, if you had cropped it right at that moon''s edge. It would be soft in real life, a the clouds and rain would dull the edges. You do have the blown out boats on the left hand side, not a lot you can do about that, as it is what it is.  But if you had done several exposures you could have stacked a less brighter one with details to replace the ones you have.  Or an alternative, if to just crop it out and just have the lower building as your left hand side, then crop the top off to make a more square but cohesive photo. One thing I do is hold my hand up when the photo is on the screen and use that a a crop tool to see if it would look better and when I first started out, I had a piece of cardboard to completly block out portions on teh side , top or bottom. I am sure in no time at all, you will be popping out immaculate images. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The picture is taken by fish eye lens. I de-fish the picture to normal film, I just want to highlight to sky that it look global!</td>', 'Originally posted by JulietNN: This was so nearly correct, but it did not come together correctly. I think for this shot, with the soft buildings (as  Neat pointed out) it would have worked with the other overlay, if you had cropped it right at that moon''s edge. It would be soft in real life, a the clouds and rain would dull the edges. You do have the blown out boats on the left hand side, not a lot you can do about that, as it is what it is.  But if you had done several exposures you could have stacked a less brighter one with details to replace the ones you have.  Or an alternative, if to just crop it out and just have the lower building as your left hand side, then crop the top off to make a more square but cohesive photo. One thing I do is hold my hand up when the photo is on the screen and use that a a crop tool to see if it would look better and when I first started out, I had a piece of cardboard to completly block out portions on teh side , top or bottom. I am sure in no time at all, you will be popping out immaculate images.  The picture is taken by fish eye lens. I de-fish the picture to normal film, I just want to highlight to sky that it look global!', '2018-08-23 03:34:35.000000', NULL, 0),
